.TH WINSOCK_INIT 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
winsock_init \- Initialize Winsock

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/socket.h>

.IB void
.IB __winsock_init(void);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fB__winsock_init\fR function is used to initialize Winsock. It ensures that Winsock is only initialized once by using a static variable to track initialization status. If Winsock is not already initialized, it calls \fBWSAStartup\fR to initialize Winsock version 2.2.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The \fB__winsock_init\fR function does not return a value.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fB__winsock_init\fR function to initialize Winsock:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/socket.h>

int main() {
    __winsock_init();
    // Your socket-related code here
    return 0;
}
.nef